# .trivyignore — CVEs the pipeline tolerates, each with evidence and a
# review date so this file does not become a dumping ground for
# silenced findings.
#
# Policy (per ADR-0032):
#   - Only CVEs with no reachable fix, or proven unreachable, go here.
#   - Every entry MUST have a comment with the reason + a review date.
#   - On every CI run, Trivy still prints these to the log — the ignore
#     only suppresses the exit-code block, not the visibility.
#   - Re-verify by scanning the image WITHOUT this file and diffing.
#
# Last reviewed: 2026-11-20 — full re-scan without this file. The 3
# fastify entries (84428/84469/84504) were removed: no longer present.

# ─── OpenSSL libssl3 in the distroless base — present, never loaded ──
# All 7 findings are in Debian's libssl3 3.0.18-1~deb12u2 inside
# gcr.io/distroless/nodejs22-debian12:nonroot. Debian has fixes
# (3.0.19–3.0.22), but the digest we pin is still Google's latest
# :nonroot build (checked 2026-11-20), so no patched base exists yet.
#
# Why this is tolerable — the library is unreachable, verified:
#   - Node does NOT use the system OpenSSL. `ldd /nodejs/bin/node`
#     lists only libc, libstdc++, libm, libgcc_s, libdl, libpthread —
#     no libssl/libcrypto. Node statically bundles its own OpenSSL
#     (process.versions.openssl = 3.5.4).
#   - Distroless has no shell, package manager or other binaries that
#     could load libssl3. Node is the only process in the container.
#
# Exit path: .github/dependabot.yml watches the base-image digest and
# opens a PR when Google ships a rebuilt :nonroot image; that PR's CI
# run shows which of these entries can go.
# Re-review: 2026-12-04
CVE-2026-28387
CVE-2026-28388
CVE-2026-28389
CVE-2026-28390
CVE-2026-31789
CVE-2026-45447
CVE-2026-84782
